      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Elmo opened a post office in 1873 and by the mid‑1880s boasted several mills, five churches, schools, and about 900 residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elmo%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1892, Elmo residents passed a resolution declaring the town a sundown town, forcing African Americans to leave.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elmo%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s population fell from 150 in 1945 to just 90 by 1990, reflecting a long‑term decline.",
